{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The length of this trip is governed by the GPS trace, which measures 22.26 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff, not by the 22.3 km figure carried on the trip record: POL-RD-01 says in terms that trip_record.actual_distance_km is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and may NOT be cited for the threshold test. The fare on EV-FARE-00528 was nevertheless billed on distance_charged_km 22.3, i.e. on the rounded copy the clause disfavours, so the charge rests on a figure the governing clause tells the tribunal not to use.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00528", "EV-TRIP-00528", "EV-FARE-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on this record excuses the distance the driver actually ran, and the rider closes those doors now. The traffic-advisory artifact for this trip is MISSING: EV-ADVIS-00528-01 has no payload, carries weight 0.0 and fired issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so no advisory can be pointed to under POL-RD-03 to exonerate any excess. The chat log for TRP-00528 (EV-CHAT-00528, complete, weight 1.0) is empty — message_count 0 — so no rider-requested detour or additional stop can be made out under POL-RD-04 either. The driver's 'normal trip, normal route' is the only thing on file in his favour.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00528-01", "EV-CHAT-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not press a distance-deviation claim, because the arithmetic does not support one and the rider will not put a number in front of the tribunal that the record contradicts. Measured on the governing trace the excess over the 22.1 km optimal is 0.16 km, or 0.72% of optimal — below both of POL-RD-01's establishment gates, which require an excess greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms AND greater than 20% of optimal. No deviation is established on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00528", "EV-TRIP-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "What is left is small, but it is arithmetic the platform has already run on its own ledger, and it is the rider's money. EV-FARE-00528 charges distance on 22.3 km and time on 38.0 min against an optimal of 22.1 km and 36.0 min, and the fare breakdown's own recomputation under POL-RD-02 prices the trip at 43.4370 against a charged_total of 44.44 — a difference of 1.0030, which rounds up to 1.05. The rider asks the tribunal to settle that line on the fare rather than leave it standing unexamined; it is the only distance-and-time correction this record will support, and it should be stated on the face of the ruling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00528", "EV-TRIP-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider also does not maintain the arithmetic pleaded in the filed claim. The trip record shows the estimate displayed at booking was 58-62 before surge, and the ledger's charged_total is 44.44 — below that figure, not above it — and the fare is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 gives the rider no quote-versus-charge difference to claim. The rider's complaint is about how this trip was billed, not about a fare that exceeded the price shown.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00528", "EV-FARE-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the present state of the record the tribunal cannot say what NO_ACTION would preserve. EV-FARE-00528 records payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, while the rider's account is that the difference was already refunded and a voucher issued. NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03 leaves exactly that conflict as it stands — the charge stays collected — whereas ESCALATE holds the disputed amount rather than collecting or refunding it. The rider asks that the amount be held for a human reviewer rather than left as a charge whose state the record does not agree on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The route-deviation threshold in POL-RD-01 is not met on the governing measurement. The GPS trace runs 22.26 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff events against a booked optimal of 22.1 km: an excess of 0.16 km, or 0.724% of the optimal distance. POL-RD-01 makes a deviation ESTABLISHED only where the excess is greater than 20% of optimal_distance_km AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms, and both gates must pass. Both fail here by more than an order of magnitude. The excess is not merely below the materiality gate, it is below the ordinary establishment gate, so no deviation exists on this trip and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the drive.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00528", "EV-TRIP-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no reading of the distance fields on which the rider succeeds. POL-RD-01 states expressly that gps_trace.trace_distance_km governs and that trip_record.actual_distance_km is a rounded convenience copy which may NOT be cited for the threshold test. On the trace figure the excess is 0.16 km; on the rounded 22.3 km copy it is 0.2 km. The two figures do not straddle the 0.8 km absolute gate the way POL-RD-01's drafting note contemplates, because neither of them approaches it. Whichever field the rider reaches for, the establishment test fails.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00528", "EV-TRIP-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace that carries the measurement is clean, so there is no gap in the record for the rider to exploit. EV-GPS-00528 records 229 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, from first fix 08:16:40 to last fix 08:54:40. None of POL-RD-07's impairment limbs fires: there is no gap over 90 seconds, no straight-line jump over 500 m and no sustained sampling interval above 30 seconds. The excess is therefore measured from an unimpaired trace, no independent corroboration is required, and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation trigger cannot fire.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and does not discharge it. Limb (a) is satisfied in form — the trip identifier TRP-00528 runs consistently through the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown, and the pickup timestamp is common to them — but limb (b) requires an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold measured from an unimpaired trace, and the derived deviation status is 'no deviation'. The burden never shifts to the driver, no exculpatory clause under POL-RD-03, POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 or POL-RD-12 needs to be run, and the rider's claim fails at the threshold it was required to cross.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00528", "EV-GPS-00528", "EV-FARE-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The residue route left open by POL-RD-01 — a billing-integrity refund under POL-RD-09(4), available whether or not a deviation exists — affords the rider nothing here. The fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines at all and an ERP total of 0.00, and no airport surcharge (this trip neither originates nor ends at an airport). Every charged line corresponds to this trip's own recorded movement: base fare 3.80, metered distance on 22.3 km, metered time on 38.0 minutes, the 1.4 surge recorded on the fare breakdown, and the 0.80 platform fee. There is no unmatched charge line for POL-RD-09(4) to correct.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00528", "EV-GPS-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "NO_ACTION is party-relative under POL-GEN-03, and on this rider-filed dispute it preserves the present payment state. The ledger records payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so no refund has in fact issued and the driver's metered fare stands intact. The rider's assertion that a support manager 'refunded the difference plus a voucher' is supported by no artifact in the bundle; on the only payment artifact before the tribunal, the charge is live and nothing has been returned.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own narrative does not survive contact with the artifacts. The claim text asserts the trip carried 'no surge', but POL-RD-02 fixes the surge multiplier on fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier and nowhere else, and that field reads 1.4. The claim text asserts a fare of 'ninety-one sixty' against an estimate of sixty, but the only fare artifact records total_charged 44.44, quoted_fare_sgd null and a distance-and-time charge built at the metered rate card — a figure lower than the estimate range carried on the trip record, not higher. No artifact in the bundle supports the figures on which the rider's complaint is constructed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00528", "EV-TRIP-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.surge_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation uplift is available and none is needed. POL-RD-06 is consulted only where POL-RD-01 records a MATERIAL deviation, or where the evidence is otherwise finely balanced; on this trace there is no deviation at all, material or otherwise. For completeness, the driver's trailing-90-day deviation flag count is 0 against 250 completed trips in the same window, so neither limb of the POL-RD-06 pattern test could be satisfied even if the clause were engaged. Limb (b)'s uplift and limb (c)'s conduct referral are simply not in play.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00528", "EV-GPS-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "None of POL-RD-10's mandatory escalation triggers fires on this record. The trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c); no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact; the timestamps do not disagree — the trace opens at 08:16:40 on the trip record's started_at and closes at 08:54:40 on its ended_at; and every charge line has a counterpart in the trace and trip record. There is no basis for holding the disputed amount rather than ruling on it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00528", "EV-GPS-00528", "EV-FARE-00528"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The bundle's one missing artifact is the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00528-01, which carries weight 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; I disclose that impairment expressly. Its absence cannot make this record incomplete, because an advisory's only function in this policy is to justify or reduce an excess that POL-RD-01 has already established, and there is no excess on this trace to reduce. No party needs the document for any fact the ruling turns on, so the absence is citable but immaterial.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00528-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute concerns trip TRP-00528 (Sembawang MRT to Suntec City Tower 2), and no route deviation is established. Under POL-RD-01 the governing distance is the GPS trace: EV-GPS-00528 records trace_distance_km of 22.26 against a booked optimal of 22.1 km — an excess of 0.16 km, or 0.72% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires an excess greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% of optimal before a deviation exists, and both gates fail by a wide margin, so the outcome is NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised. The trace is unimpaired (229 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gap over 90 seconds), so POL-RD-07's consequences and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation trigger are not engaged. Rider, your request for the SGD 1.05 difference the fare breakdown computes (charged_total 44.44 less a recomputed fare of 43.4370) is refused: POL-RD-02 runs only 'where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01,' and none is. That recomputation is arithmetic on a remedy whose precondition is unmet, so the charge stands. Your point that the fare was billed on the rounded 22.3 km trip-record copy rather than the governing 22.26 km trace is accepted, but it changes the distance calculation by 0.04 km and moves neither establishment gate. Rider, on your request to hold the amount for a human reviewer: no POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The trip identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare breakdown; the trace is unimpaired; no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact; the pickup and dropoff timestamps agree; and no charge line is unmatched. Your account that a support manager already refunded the difference and issued a voucher is supported by no artifact in the bundle — the only payment record, EV-FARE-00528, shows payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. POL-RD-10(7) escalation requires both sides to be supported by admissible, mutually contradictory evidence, and a bare narrative set against a single ledger figure is not that. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION leaves the present state standing. There is no billing-integrity defect under POL-RD-09(4): the fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines (ERP total 0.00) and no airport surcharge, and every charged line — base fare 3.80, metered distance and time at the surge multiplier of 1.4 recorded on the fare breakdown, and the 0.80 platform fee — corresponds to this trip's recorded movement. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00528-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is citable as an absence but immaterial, since an advisory only justifies or reduces an excess and there is none. No referral arises: with no material deviation POL-RD-06 is not engaged, and the driver profile shows no trailing-90-day deviation pattern (0 flags against 250 completed trips) in any event; no billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4) either. Confidence is 0.90; the deciding fact rests on artifacts at full weight (EV-GPS-00528 and EV-TRIP-00528, both 1.0)."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
